Mario Stargard wrote:
> -----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----
> Hash: SHA1
> 
> Shiva MahaDeva wrote:
> | In my job I need make a backup from area /usr/atl/*2002* and area
> | /etc/dbs/*sx*
> | Which vdump command must I issue to make a valid backup ?
> | Where could I get a good tutorial about vdump ?
> | Thanks in advance.
> 
> The vdump manpage is very detailed.  You don't mention what version of
> Tru64 you're using.  Version 4 and 5 vdump are a little different.
> 
> If you want the backups to be portable, use GNU tar.

Not to mention that "vdump", although capable of backing up just one 
directory sub-tree, is more suited for file system backups. For partial 
backups, tar is much better (or GNU tar).

To answer the original question, it would require 2 commands:

# vdump -0 -C -N -D /etc/dbs/
# vdump -0 -C -D /usr/atl/

Note that those commands will backup desired files *plus all other files 
in those dirs*. "vdump" cannot backup a set of files, but rather a 
directory, it's subdirectories and all the files in that sub-tree. What 
you need is "tar". Period.

Nix.


