vince wrote:

> I have an oracle server running Tru64 5.1A and it crashed this
> morning.  I don't really know where to start on troubleshooting this.
> 
> I ran crashdc but the information there really didn't help me as I
> don't know what I am looking at.

It looks like you ran crashdc on the running image, not the crash.  But 
you really don't need to do this at all, it's done automatically at boot 
time on a system crash.  Look in /var/adm/crash/ - there should be three 
files with the same number suffix, for example, 0:

crash-data.0
vmunix.0
vmzcore.0

crash-data.0 is the output from crashdc run against vmunix.0 and 
vmzcore.0.  The numbers increment on every crash.

-Brian



